# Retired URLs, kept honest.
#
# Cloudflare Workers static assets parses this file automatically; no wrangler
# configuration is involved. Every rule below is a real 301, not a meta refresh,
# so a link that has been shared or indexed keeps working and search engines
# learn the new address rather than seeing the old one disappear.
#
# The site's earlier blog described an architecture Epicenter no longer has:
# one folder of plain text, apps automatically sharing memory, a quickstart for
# a package that has since been replaced. Leaving those posts up would mean
# publishing claims we know to be wrong, so the articles are gone and their
# addresses point at the writing that replaced them.

/blog                             /writing/   301
/blog/*                           /writing/   301

# A prototype landing page and a scratch wordmark page, neither of which was
# ever linked from the site.
/archive/index-v1                 /           301
/archive/*                        /           301
/logo                             /           301
